research_rationale:
EO 12358 (1982-04-14), 47 FR 16311 machine text. Sec. 4(b): "The Commission, shall terminate one year from this date" (1983-04-14). EO 12415 (1983-04-05, held APP text and FR original) amended 4(b) to "The Commission shall terminate on December 31, 1983." Effective date 1983-12-31 is the as-extended stated date. EO 12376 raised membership only. Dossier gap on EO 12553 is the 1986-02-25 revocation, read directly: after the end.
Member checks: {"earlier_end_check":"Searched: dossier chain (2 events), EDGES (EO 12376, EO 12415, EO 12553 revocation 1986-02-25), held corpus for the Commission name (EO 12358, 12376, 12415, 12553). The only dated end is EO 12415 sec. 4(b) as amended; the 1986 revocation postdates it. No earlier end held.","independent_command_check":"No independent command: functions, administration and general provisions all concern the Commission.","savings_check":"Read the order: no savings or exceptions.","scope_check":"Eleven dossier clauses (secs. 1 to 4); every one concerns the Presidential Commission on Drunk Driving. Sec. 4(b) terminates the Commission and nothing survives it. The amendment EO 12415 is a clean replacement of 4(b)."}
Fixer note (2026-10-20): first_end and whole_order_end now cite the held official FR text of EO 12415 (EO_12415.txt, 48 FR 15117) as the source of the date; EO 12415 and EO 12376 added as later events from held official FR texts.

EO 12528 (1985-08-08), 50 FR 32389 machine text. Sec. 4(a): "The Board shall terminate two years from the date of this Order, unless sooner extended." (1987-08-08). EO 12604 (1987-08-05, held APP text) replaced 4(a): "The Board shall terminate on July 1, 1989, unless sooner extended." Effective date 1989-07-01 is the as-extended stated date. EO 12692 (1989-09-29) sec. 3(f) revokes the order as amended after the end.
Member checks: {"earlier_end_check":"Searched: dossier chain (2 events), EDGES (EO 12604, EO 12692 revocation), EO 12692 read (revocation 90 days after the end), held corpus for the Board name. No earlier end and no later extension held.","independent_command_check":"No independent command: all provisions create, fund or administer the Board.","savings_check":"Read the order: only \"unless sooner extended\"; no savings.","scope_check":"Nine dossier clauses (secs. 1 to 4); all concern the Presidential Board of Advisors on Private Sector Initiatives. Sec. 4(a) terminates the Board and nothing survives it."}
